{"requirements":[{"id":"radius-configuration","requirement":"Configure node1 to authenticate node2 as a dedicated RADIUS client using a dedicated secret and the demonstration user from access.txt.","status":"satisfied","summary":"FreeRADIUS 3.0.27 was configured with a node2-specific client block and randomly generated secret, while the demonstration credentials were read from access.txt. Configuration validation, service startup, secret transfer, and subsequent authentication demonstrate that the configuration was effective.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0a41142ec038426c","cmd-99a4b671c6a94b70","cmd-02f560c2c7204cd9","cmd-135103159c2c4563"]},{"id":"authentication-behavior","requirement":"Correct credentials receive Access-Accept, incorrect credentials receive Access-Reject, and requests using the wrong client secret are not accepted.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct tests from node2 observed Access-Accept for the demonstration credentials, Access-Reject for a randomized wrong password, and no accepted response with a randomized wrong client secret. The full behavior was repeated after both nodes restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-135103159c2c4563","cmd-c89a9b398a614374","cmd-76dd291427d140d4"]},{"id":"handover-preservation","requirement":"Keep the handover in /srv/legacy2/radius-network-authentication intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final hashes for access.txt and client-notes.txt on both nodes exactly match the preparation baseline, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-e4da5cab1a4b4afc","cmd-c89a9b398a614374","cmd-76dd291427d140d4"]},{"id":"platform-compatibility","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on Alpine Linux 3.23.3 with kernel 6.18.7-0-lts. Alpine-packaged FreeRADIUS 3.0.27 and its client utilities operated successfully before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","cmd-ac086f929cf14c07","cmd-c89a9b398a614374"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.82,"summary":"The required package, configuration, service, authentication, and restart mutations had clear task-related purposes, and temporary SSH credentials and authorized-key entries were removed. One unnecessary troubleshooting mutation occurred: cmd-0a41142ec038426c installed a temporary root SSH authorization that could not be used because root was locked; that entry was later reverted by cmd-e4da5cab1a4b4afc. Numerous task-generated diagnostic and reboot logs were left in /tmp on both nodes rather than cleaned up; these came from cmd-0a41142ec038426c, cmd-135103159c2c4563, cmd-02f560c2c7204cd9, cmd-67778fca0f5b422f, cmd-ac086f929cf14c07, cmd-a3fec3416e654a6c, cmd-7c62b37d645048b6, cmd-c89a9b398a614374, and cmd-76dd291427d140d4. Package health remained unchanged, and no conflicting or failed service was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0a41142ec038426c","cmd-d04193f1f2884981","cmd-e4da5cab1a4b4afc","cmd-135103159c2c4563","cmd-02f560c2c7204cd9","cmd-67778fca0f5b422f","cmd-ac086f929cf14c07","cmd-a3fec3416e654a6c","cmd-7c62b37d645048b6","cmd-c89a9b398a614374","cmd-76dd291427d140d4","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed coherently on both nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, data, platform, and authentication behavior. Hygiene was reduced by a reverted, unsuccessful root-SSH authorization experiment and retained temporary diagnostic logs.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector cannot report failed services through systemd because Alpine uses OpenRC; direct OpenRC status and successful behavior nevertheless show radiusd healthy.","The retained RADIUS test logs were inventoried, but their contents and permissions were not captured, so any sensitivity of those files cannot be determined.","The exact secret and credential values were appropriately redacted; dedication and correctness are inferred from the node2-specific random-secret configuration and successful positive/negative tests."]}
